.TH CLIPPED 1 "September 2026" "clipped 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipped \- clipboard history manager for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipped
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Clipped
records the text and images you copy and lets you paste any of them back into
the application you were using. It runs in the background on GNOME (Wayland)
using desktop portals for clipboard access, the global shortcut and autostart,
and includes a searchable emoji and symbol picker.
.PP
Press
.B Super+Shift+V
to open it from any application. Type to filter, use the arrow keys to move,
and press
.B Enter
to paste. The shortcut can be changed in Settings \(en Keyboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-gapplication\-service
Start in the background without showing the window. This is how the login
autostart entry and D-Bus activation launch it.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the standard GApplication options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/clipped/history.db
Clipboard history (SQLite). Images are stored as PNG files in
.IR ~/.local/share/clipped/images/ .
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.djshiye.Clipped.desktop
Autostart entry managed through the Background portal.
.SH SETTINGS
Preferences are stored in GSettings under
.BR io.github.djshiye.Clipped .
.SH BUGS
Report at https://github.com/djshiye/clipped-fedora/issues
.SH AUTHOR
djshiye
